    "text": "(2) Merging record-local graphs: If the version order can be de- termined for all records in the write set while keeping the graph acyclic, 𝑡 then merges the record-local graph for each record in 𝑖 the read set into its transaction-local graph. Each time 𝑡 merges a 𝑖 record-local graph, it checks the acyclicity of the resulting graph and identifies all its followers. If a follower of 𝑡 exists, 𝑖 𝑡 merges 𝑖 record-local graphs of the records read or written by that follower and repeats identifying its followers and merging the record-local graphs. If no cycle is found in 𝑆𝐺 ( 𝑠, 𝑡 ) , which is obtained by merg- 𝑖 ing all graphs on records read or written by all followers, 𝑡 proceeds 𝑖 to the finalizing phase for committing."
  },
